/// The quotient of two integers is made where the operator is found: an
/// integer where they divide (but -0 for zero by a negative divisor), a
/// double kept in the Value where its bits are few (the halves and the
/// quarters), and as before by the doubles otherwise. Integers that
/// divide, of every sign; zero divided, and a zero divisor of either
/// sign; halves, quarters and smaller parts to the ends of the safe
/// integers; thirds and tenths; an integer quotient used as a key, an
/// index, a length and a count, and a kept quotient found as the Number
/// it is in a Map, a Set and an Array; the forms a division is written
/// in, compound ones among them; doubles, operands that are converted,
/// BigInts and Symbols; two grids, one against the remainder and the
/// product and one against the same division made of doubles; many
/// turns. What is expected is what Node prints for the same script.
#[test]
fn a_quotient_of_two_integers_is_what_the_steps_give() {
    std::thread::Builder::new()
        .stack_size(8 << 20)
        .spawn(integers_divided)
        .expect("thread")
        .join()
        .expect("checks");
}

